    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-email-domain blocklist rule for the PetClinic Spring Boot app, following the existing validation conventions (mirroring `PostcodeValidator`/`InvalidPostcodeException`):\n\n1. **`DisposableEmailValidator`** (`util/`) \u2014 extracts the domain after the last `@` and rejects (case-insensitively) when it's on the fixed blocklist: `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`. A `null`/empty email is accepted, keeping the contract backward-compatible.\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailException`** (`util/`) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown on a blocked domain.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 calls `DisposableEmailValidator.validate(...)` on the normalized (lower-cased) email in both the create (`addOwner`) and update (`updateOwner`) paths.\n\n4. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `DisposableEmailException` to **400 Bad Request**, consistent with the other validation handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`) now passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nNote: this repo isn't a git repository, so there's nothing to commit.",
